01:00:40.290 --> 01:00:42.290
but also a coming.

272
01:00:42.290 --> 01:00:46.290
40 years is often significant in the Bible.

273
01:00:46.290 --> 01:00:50.290
So I see this month as celebrating what has been

274
01:00:51.290 --> 01:00:54.290
but also stepping into something new.

275
01:00:54.290 --> 01:00:58.290
In the Bible, you see that 40 years is often a significant period.

276
01:01:03.290 --> 01:01:07.290
40 years, 40 days is often a time of testing.

277
01:01:11.290 --> 01:01:15.290
And I would like to say that the Lord has tested this house time and again.

278
01:01:16.290 --> 01:01:20.290
Hold the babies tightly, we are really coming to them.

279
01:01:24.290 --> 01:01:26.290
The Lord has tested this house.

280
01:01:26.290 --> 01:01:29.290
If you don't think this is true, that is what He does.

281
01:01:29.290 --> 01:01:31.290
He tests what is in the heart.

282
01:01:31.290 --> 01:01:33.290
He tests over and over, for 40 years.

283
01:01:33.290 --> 01:01:37.290
Oh yes, there have been tests to see what was in us.

284
01:01:37.290 --> 01:01:41.290
I have not been here for 40 years, but what has been here. Amen.

285
01:01:50.290 --> 01:01:51.290
He sifts.

286
01:01:53.290 --> 01:01:54.290
He removes.

287
01:01:56.290 --> 01:01:57.290
He plants.

288
01:01:58.290 --> 01:01:59.290
He builds.

289
01:02:00.290 --> 01:02:01.290
He is strategic.

290
01:02:04.290 --> 01:02:09.290
For if you look at it honestly, this place is a miracle.

291
01:02:16.290 --> 01:02:20.290
Look at yourself and say, how can it be that we are here like this?

292
01:02:20.290 --> 01:02:23.290
It is a miracle because the Spirit is at work.

293
01:02:27.290 --> 01:02:30.290
And at the same time, we must not only look back,

294
01:02:30.290 --> 01:02:33.290
but we must also look to the present and press forward.

295
01:02:42.290 --> 01:02:47.290
So in the month of May, we will increase the intercession times.

296
01:02:48.290 --> 01:02:52.290
And in this month of May, we will increase our prayer time

297
01:02:52.290 --> 01:02:55.290
and we will also meet together every Thursday.

298
01:03:01.290 --> 01:03:06.290
And I want to speak about intercession and the role of God's people in it.

299
01:03:18.290 --> 01:03:23.290
Also last week, last Thursday, when we were together in intercession.

300
01:03:27.290 --> 01:03:31.290
I felt again that the Lord said, it is time for that intercession to increase.

301
01:03:37.290 --> 01:03:42.290
So I want to dive into the Bible and see what intercession is about

302
01:03:42.290 --> 01:03:44.290
and what is the role of God's people in it?

303
01:03:48.290 --> 01:03:59.290
In Greek, the word intercession means to fully achieve your goal.

304
01:04:03.290 --> 01:04:06.290
It means to hit the target with your arrow.

305
01:04:09.290 --> 01:04:11.290
If you know something about the Greek language.

306
01:04:18.290 --> 01:04:24.290
When I read that intercession means that you place a shot in the target, it immediately made me think of something else.

307
01:04:36.290 --> 01:04:41.290
For the word sin in Greek means to miss the mark.

308
01:04:48.290 --> 01:04:59.290
When it says in Romans that all have sinned, it means that we have all missed our shot.

309
01:05:04.290 --> 01:05:09.290
In other words, outside of Christ, your life misses its purpose.

310
01:05:12.290 --> 01:05:16.290
For that is sin, then we are not in line with God's plan.

311
01:05:16.290 --> 01:05:17.290
It makes sense.

312
01:05:22.290 --> 01:05:25.290
But once you are grafted into Christ.

313
01:05:31.290 --> 01:05:38.290
Then God says, at this moment you have the opportunity to aim fully at the target again.

314
01:05:40.290 --> 01:05:41.290
Think of Jesus.

315
01:05:43.290 --> 01:05:45.290
He lived a life of prayer.

316
01:05:46.290 --> 01:05:47.290
And of intercession.

317
01:05:51.290 --> 01:05:54.290
And He did not do that from a religious motive.

318
01:05:59.290 --> 01:06:03.290
Not like, I am a good person because I spent some time in prayer this morning.

319
01:06:04.290 --> 01:06:13.290
The Son of God kept His connection with God alive through prayer, for He needed that connection to then do the will of the Father.

320
01:06:25.290 --> 01:06:27.290
So if we are in Christ.

321
01:06:28.290 --> 01:06:31.290
Then it is prayer that keeps us focused on the goal.

322
01:06:45.290 --> 01:06:52.290
I must remain connected to Him to know what the purpose of my life is and to be able to aim for it.

323
01:06:53.290 --> 01:06:55.290
It is being fully engaged with God.

324
01:07:07.290 --> 01:07:11.290
So we see Jesus as the perfect Son, and He fully achieves His purpose in His life.

325
01:07:22.290 --> 01:07:38.290
So when we look at intercession, it is not an option, but it is the way in which we can fully reach the purpose and will of the Father in our lives.

326
01:07:38.290 --> 01:07:53.290
So it means hitting the mark completely, and it also means someone who stands in the breach, jumps into the gap.

327
01:08:09.290 --> 01:08:22.290
Every time there are problems in the people of Israel, God calls someone, a prophet, an intercessor, someone who can jump into that gap.

328
01:08:22.290 --> 01:08:28.290
Someone who stands between the reality in which we now live and what we are heading towards.

329
01:08:38.290 --> 01:08:46.290
And that person stands there and reminds the people of what God has said, but he also speaks the words of God back to God as a priest.

330
01:08:51.290 --> 01:08:55.290
If you look at Abraham, he is called a prophet and an intercessor.

331
01:09:09.290 --> 01:09:18.290
Moses was not just a good leader; he was a prophet who stood before God and interceded with God on behalf of the people.

332
01:09:18.290 --> 01:09:23.290
And perhaps the woman I have spoken with the women over the last year is Esther.

333
01:09:23.290 --> 01:09:28.290
Esther, in essence, took on the role of an intercessor.

334
01:09:28.290 --> 01:09:35.290
Takes the voice of the Lord, stands in the gap for the people of Israel to consider the crisis.

335
01:09:35.290 --> 01:09:40.290
And with the women, we have often talked about Esther, and she was also an intercessor.

336
01:09:40.290 --> 01:09:47.290
She stood in that gap and made intercession for Israel.

337
01:09:54.290 --> 01:10:00.290
So you stand before the Lord and you are on earth, but you find yourself in the gates of heaven.

338
01:10:04.290 --> 01:10:08.290
And that gives God the space to move on earth.

339
01:10:11.290 --> 01:10:15.290
And then you might think, God can do whatever He wants, because He is God.

340
01:10:22.290 --> 01:10:25.290
Why then must I pray and have an ear to hear?

341
01:10:25.290 --> 01:10:28.290
That is simple, because He desires to do it with us.

342
01:10:33.290 --> 01:10:37.290
And not only that, God has given the earth to Adam.

343
01:10:41.290 --> 01:10:46.290
And that means that we as humans take responsibility for this earth.

344
01:10:49.290 --> 01:10:52.290
Many people blame God for what happens in the world.

345
01:10:53.290 --> 01:10:55.290
Christians blame God.

346
01:10:55.290 --> 01:11:05.290
And they do not realize that this is an immature response, because God has called us to do here on earth what He desires from us.

347
01:11:17.290 --> 01:11:19.290
What did Jesus do in the wilderness?

348
01:11:21.290 --> 01:11:23.290
He overcame Satan.

349
01:11:24.290 --> 01:11:25.290
But what did He do?

350
01:11:31.290 --> 01:11:34.290
He takes back the dominion as man.

351
01:11:35.290 --> 01:11:37.290
Adam lost it.

352
01:11:42.290 --> 01:11:45.290
Adam lost that responsibility, he became passive.

353
01:11:45.290 --> 01:11:49.290
And men, if you adopt a passive stance, then you are not living in the will of God.

354
01:11:54.290 --> 01:11:55.290
He was there.

355
01:11:56.290 --> 01:11:57.290
He had a mouth.

356
01:11:58.290 --> 01:12:00.290
He could have said something.

357
01:12:03.290 --> 01:12:07.290
He knew that God had given them one command that they would not do.

358
01:12:09.290 --> 01:12:11.290
In the garden, there was only one thing.

359
01:12:12.290 --> 01:12:13.290
And they messed it up.

360
01:12:14.290 --> 01:12:16.290
Now there are thousands of laws, but back then it was one thing.

361
01:12:17.290 --> 01:12:19.290
If you do this, then you will be with me.

362
01:12:20.290 --> 01:12:21.290
Are you still following me?

363
01:12:26.290 --> 01:12:32.290
And what Jesus shows in Matthew 4 is that He says, I will restore the dominion as man.

364
01:12:33.290 --> 01:12:40.290
And what Jesus shows in Matthew 4 is that He says, I will restore the dominion as man.

365
01:12:40.290 --> 01:12:47.290
And what Jesus shows in Matthew 4 is that He says, I will restore the dominion of men.

366
01:12:50.290 --> 01:12:51.290
I will not fall for Satan.

367
01:12:59.290 --> 01:13:04.290
I do not agree with what is happening there. I will do the will of the Father through the Word of the Lord.

368
01:13:10.290 --> 01:13:17.290
And what we receive with intercessions is that we again have the opportunity to reign.

369
01:13:28.290 --> 01:13:29.290
1 Peter 2

370
01:13:33.290 --> 01:13:38.290
And I want to explain that intercession is really for every saint.

371
01:13:41.290 --> 01:13:45.290
Every born-again believer has a role in prayer.

372
01:13:49.290 --> 01:13:53.290
Being an intercessor is not part of the fivefold ministry.

373
01:14:01.290 --> 01:14:09.290
It is not a part of the pastors and shepherds and teachers, for we are all called to pray.

374
01:14:11.290 --> 01:14:12.290
Amen.

375
01:14:13.290 --> 01:14:19.290
An apostle who does not remain connected to the will of the Lord will not be an apostle for long.

376
01:14:24.290 --> 01:14:29.290
I spoke with some people last night and they said, we pray that you have good people around you.

377
01:14:29.290 --> 01:14:34.290
I said, do you know how we do this? We do it because we remain so.

378
01:14:34.290 --> 01:14:40.290
That is the only way, to be honest. That is the only possibility to stay with the Lord.

379
01:14:47.290 --> 01:14:49.290
In 1 Peter 2

380
01:14:52.290 --> 01:14:55.290
Peter says, now God makes you a spiritual house.

381
01:14:56.290 --> 01:15:01.290
There it says, let yourselves be a spiritual temple.

382
01:15:06.290 --> 01:15:10.290
If you are a living stone, then you are part of what God is doing.

383
01:15:13.290 --> 01:15:16.290
And it is a spiritual temple, for the Spirit lives in each of you.

384
01:15:26.290 --> 01:15:29.290
And it is not enough to just be a Christian at home.

385
01:15:29.290 --> 01:15:32.290
God does things in the whole that He cannot do with us alone.

386
01:15:37.290 --> 01:15:39.290
You are now a holy priesthood.

387
01:15:44.290 --> 01:15:48.290
And in the old days this was not possible, but through Christians this is now possible.

388
01:15:49.290 --> 01:15:53.290
And you will bring spiritual sacrifices to God.

389
01:15:59.290 --> 01:16:01.290
And these will be pleasing to Him.

390
01:16:05.290 --> 01:16:07.290
And it is a sacrifice to bring prayer.

391
01:16:09.290 --> 01:16:12.290
It is difficult to bring people into prayer.

392
01:16:15.290 --> 01:16:17.290
It is difficult to bring people to fasting.

393
01:16:19.290 --> 01:16:22.290
But if you understand that God has made us to do this.

394
01:16:27.290 --> 01:16:30.290
And that He says, it is a sacrifice that is pleasing to me.

395
01:16:40.290 --> 01:16:47.290
And if you understand that it is part of God bringing His will to fruition in your life and in your whole life.

396
01:16:48.290 --> 01:16:49.290
In your whole generation.

397
01:16:53.290 --> 01:16:55.290
So the believers together.

398
01:16:58.290 --> 01:17:00.290
What we do is stand before the Lord.

399
01:17:02.290 --> 01:17:04.290
And we agree with the will of God.

400
01:17:06.290 --> 01:17:08.290
We agree with His Word.

401
01:17:19.290 --> 01:17:21.290
We take our responsibility as priests.

402
01:17:22.290 --> 01:17:25.290
And we say Lord, we want to see your will happen here on earth.

403
01:17:26.290 --> 01:17:28.290
Lord, do what you want to do.

404
01:17:32.290 --> 01:17:36.290
The most important ministry of the church in the New Testament is prayer and intercession.

405
01:17:38.290 --> 01:17:40.290
Regardless of what your role is.

406
01:17:42.290 --> 01:17:43.290
If you are a baker.

407
01:17:45.290 --> 01:17:46.290
Then pray.

408
01:17:49.290 --> 01:17:55.290
If you are a teacher at school, then you are also an intercessor, because you intervene in that place.

409
01:18:08.290 --> 01:18:11.290
God places us in the world exactly where we are.

410
01:18:12.290 --> 01:18:16.290
And then we come together and in both situations we ask God to intervene.

411
01:18:19.290 --> 01:18:23.290
For intercession and prayer with the Lord, that influences everything.

412
01:18:34.290 --> 01:18:42.290
It is the revelation that God wants us to trust in Him through the Spirit and to be dependent on Him to do what He has called us to do.

413
01:18:43.290 --> 01:18:45.290
The power can be found nowhere else.

414
01:19:02.290 --> 01:19:08.290
When we say things like not by might or not by power, but by your Spirit, what does that actually mean?

415
01:19:09.290 --> 01:19:11.290
How do you interpret that?

416
01:19:20.290 --> 01:19:25.290
It is written in the context of rebuilding the house of prayer in Zechariah.

417
01:19:33.290 --> 01:19:35.290
I really want to call us to something this month.

418
01:19:39.290 --> 01:19:47.290
A large part of your life as a Christian will be illogical until you grasp this revelation.

419
01:19:56.290 --> 01:20:05.290
For it is in that place with the Lord where you will see that He says, okay, now you will hit the target that I have set for you.

420
01:20:06.290 --> 01:20:08.290
In 1 Timothy 2

421
01:20:15.290 --> 01:20:20.290
There Paul writes to Timothy and he calls for all kinds of prayer for all kinds of people.

422
01:20:26.290 --> 01:20:30.290
Paul calls the church to be engaged in all kinds of prayer.

423
01:20:36.290 --> 01:20:44.290
And he speaks to Timothy and to the whole congregation and he says, listen, this is your role to bring all kinds of prayer for others.

424
01:20:45.290 --> 01:20:54.290
Not just the prophets or the apostles or the youth, but everyone who finds themselves in the gathering of God.

425
01:20:55.290 --> 01:21:04.290
For it is a privilege, it is an honor, it is an honor that you find yourself in the gathering of God.

426
01:21:09.290 --> 01:21:19.290
And if you find yourself in the gathering of God, then it is an honor that you find yourself in the gathering of God.

427
01:21:25.290 --> 01:21:34.290
It is the God of heaven who looks again at people to govern the earth.

428
01:21:36.290 --> 01:21:43.290
And to do it in His way, in line with His Word, in line with the covenant.

429
01:21:43.290 --> 01:21:55.290
In Joel 2 we see that the prophet writes about a time of fasting and prayer.

430
01:22:00.290 --> 01:22:05.290
And then he receives the command from God to gather all people together.

431
01:22:14.290 --> 01:22:19.290
And it is a very interesting piece, for there everyone is truly called.

432
01:22:19.290 --> 01:22:25.290
Families, households, even those with newborns, everyone is called to come.

433
01:22:25.290 --> 01:22:27.290
And is God there common?

434
01:22:27.290 --> 01:22:32.290
And then he receives the command from God to gather all people together.

435
01:22:32.290 --> 01:22:37.290
And it is a very interesting piece, for there everyone is truly called.

436
01:22:37.290 --> 01:22:42.290
Families, households, even those with newborns, everyone is called to come.

437
01:22:42.290 --> 01:22:44.290
And is God there common?

438
01:22:57.290 --> 01:23:08.290
What God says here, and that is so beautiful, is that everyone, from the highest to the lowest,

439
01:23:08.290 --> 01:23:15.290
everyone who comes together carries something that can bring about change.

440
01:23:19.290 --> 01:23:22.290
And it is a sacrifice, but it is also an honor and a privilege.

441
01:23:27.290 --> 01:23:37.290
And in connection with this, it is stated that God desires that all will be saved.

442
01:23:40.290 --> 01:23:43.290
And that all will know the truth.

443
01:23:47.290 --> 01:23:54.290
Thus, the intercession of the believers is directly linked to souls entering the kingdom.

444
01:23:58.290 --> 01:24:10.290
If you pray for various people, you will see that God moves and brings souls into the kingdom.

445
01:24:14.290 --> 01:24:19.290
And in times of crisis, it is important that intercession increases.

446
01:24:20.290 --> 01:24:29.290
In 2 Chronicles 7, we see that Solomon is building the temple.

447
01:24:31.290 --> 01:24:34.290
And that project was started by his father David.

448
01:24:42.290 --> 01:24:46.290
At this moment in time, there is no crisis in Israel.

449
01:24:47.290 --> 01:24:49.290
It was a time of peace.

450
01:24:53.290 --> 01:24:56.290
And they had just completed that beautiful temple.

451
01:25:01.290 --> 01:25:04.290
And at the end of that dedication of Solomon,

452
01:25:11.290 --> 01:25:14.290
in the night thereafter, God speaks again to Solomon.

453
01:25:16.290 --> 01:25:22.290
It was actually interesting for me three years ago, when the Lord brought 2 Chronicles 7, before everything broke out.

454
01:25:22.290 --> 01:25:26.290
He said, I want you to look again at 2 Chronicles 7.

455
01:25:31.290 --> 01:25:35.290
And in the time of building and peace, the Lord says,

456
01:25:35.290 --> 01:25:38.290
but if and when a crisis comes,

457
01:25:39.290 --> 01:25:43.290
and in that time of building and that time of peace, the Lord says,

458
01:25:43.290 --> 01:25:45.290
if then the crisis comes,

459
01:25:51.290 --> 01:25:55.290
they are celebrating and then the Lord says, okay, if you forget me again,

460
01:25:58.290 --> 01:26:01.290
when you go into easy mode,

461
01:26:02.290 --> 01:26:03.290
for that happens.

462
01:26:05.290 --> 01:26:07.290
For He knows us, He knows the heart of people.

463
01:26:09.290 --> 01:26:13.290
He says, when that happens, when you turn away from me.

464
01:26:15.290 --> 01:26:17.290
When you start to worship other gods.

465
01:26:22.290 --> 01:26:26.290
When you do not take care of the temple in the way I ask of you.

466
01:26:30.290 --> 01:26:34.290
Then God already gives the blueprint to Solomon before it happens.

467
01:26:39.290 --> 01:26:43.290
Of the plan of how Israel can return to God when that crisis breaks out.

468
01:26:52.290 --> 01:26:56.290
And throughout the Bible we see that crises do not come out of nowhere,

469
01:26:56.290 --> 01:26:59.290
but crises come every time people turn away from God.

470
01:27:00.290 --> 01:27:04.290
And God says, I will give you the solution, the means against it, in advance.

471
01:27:18.290 --> 01:27:20.290
They are joyfully celebrating, everything is going well.

472
01:27:20.290 --> 01:27:24.290
They say, Lord, we have built a beautiful temple for you, let us celebrate.

473
01:27:29.290 --> 01:27:33.290
And then God says, when that crisis comes, when the whole financial world is turned upside down,

474
01:27:33.290 --> 01:27:35.290
when the locusts come, when the crisis is there.

475
01:27:49.290 --> 01:27:50.290
When sickness comes.

476
01:27:54.290 --> 01:27:57.290
And when you see that morality is declining.

477
01:28:00.290 --> 01:28:02.290
Israel, then you are worshiping the wrong things.

478
01:28:05.290 --> 01:28:06.290
God speaks to His people.

479
01:28:12.290 --> 01:28:16.290
God speaks to His people, He does not speak to governments, unless they are saved.

480
01:28:16.290 --> 01:28:19.290
He speaks to His people to intervene.

481
01:28:23.290 --> 01:28:26.290
And he says, listen, when this happens, you have turned away from me.

482
01:28:29.290 --> 01:28:30.290
It doesn't just happen.

483
01:28:35.290 --> 01:28:38.290
It happens because people do not worship the God of Israel.

484
01:28:42.290 --> 01:28:45.290
And he says, this is the blueprint, come and seek me.

485
01:28:47.290 --> 01:28:48.290
Come and fast.

486
01:28:50.290 --> 01:28:52.290
Put on your sackcloth.

487
01:28:54.290 --> 01:28:55.290
Yes, that is indeed very intense.

488
01:28:56.290 --> 01:28:58.290
Have you seen the crisis in the land?

489
01:29:00.290 --> 01:29:02.290
Do you think it can solve itself?

490
01:29:07.290 --> 01:29:09.290
I have given you authority over the earth.

491
01:29:16.290 --> 01:29:20.290
We do not understand the role we can play in this hour of history.

492
01:29:21.290 --> 01:29:22.290
It is in our hands.

493
01:29:26.290 --> 01:29:30.290
And then you say, yes, but I don't have that power at all.

494
01:29:30.290 --> 01:29:35.290
And that's true, but God does have it and he is looking for people he can use on earth at this moment.

495
01:29:39.290 --> 01:29:42.290
And he delights in using you in your weakness.

496
01:29:46.290 --> 01:29:52.290
For then we know that we did not do it, that we only returned and placed our trust in the Lord.

497
01:29:53.290 --> 01:29:54.290
He gets all the glory.

498
01:29:55.290 --> 01:29:58.290
A whole lot of weak people decide to hold back and think.

499
01:29:58.290 --> 01:30:00.290
They don't even feel it, but they do it with independence.

500
01:30:00.290 --> 01:30:02.290
And they say, yes, Lord, do your will.

501
